  "methodNotes": {
    "pty": "python3 pty, 24x100, child session leader with controlling pty; stderr shares the terminal stream; steps: type the name at the prompt, then wait for the `[campfire] HTTP …` listener line and send a real SIGINT (\\u0003) after a short fixed delay so the signal cannot race the shutdown-handler registration; frames are the raw stream text (CRLF line endings; expectation matching normalizes \\r\\n to \\n)",
    "ptyTermios": "check `termiosRestored` is recorded false in every PTY case, including clean exit-0 runs: on macOS, tcgetattr on the pty slave fails with ENOTTY once the session leader has exited, so the post-exit snapshot is unreadable. This is a driver limitation, not a dirty-terminal observation.",
    "piped": "spawnSync with piped stdin/stdout/stderr; no terminal anywhere",
    "daemon": "detached child; SIGINT to its process group; stderr/stdout collected"
  },
  "maskingRules": "see BASELINE_PIN.md — cft-shaped credential tokens -> [redacted]; cfe-shaped invitation secrets -> [one-time-credential: redacted]; absolute /Users, /private, /var/folders, /tmp paths -> [path]; loopback ports -> [port]; ISO timestamps -> [timestamp]; UUIDs -> [uuid]; object ids (<prefix>_<16 hex>) -> <prefix>_[id]"
}
